# University Database Management System (SQL Project)

# Project Overview

This project is a **University Database Management System** created using SQL.
It manages students, departments, courses, instructors, and enrollments.


# Database Name

`universitydb`



##  Tables Used

### 1. Departments

* Department_id (Primary Key)
* Department_name

### 2. Students

* Student_id (Primary Key)
* Firstname
* Lastname
* Email (Unique)
* Birthdate
* Enrollment_date

### 3. Courses

* Course_id (Primary Key)
* Course_name
* Department_id (Foreign Key)
* Credits

### 4. Instructors

* Instructor_id (Primary Key)
* Firstname
* Lastname
* Email (Unique)
* Department_id (Foreign Key)
* Salary

### 5. Enrollments

* Enrollmentid (Primary Key)
* Student_id (Foreign Key)
* Course_id (Foreign Key)
* Enrollment_date


##  Key Features

* Uses Primary Key and Foreign Key relationships
* Supports CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete)
* Uses joins, subqueries, and functions
* Includes real-world university data


##  CRUD Operations

### Create (Insert)

sql
INSERT INTO Students VALUES (11, 'Prince', 'Mali', 'email@email.com', '2000-01-01', '2024-01-01');


### Read (Select)

sql
SELECT * FROM Students;


###  Update

sql
UPDATE Students 
SET Email = 'new@email.com'
WHERE Student_id = 11;


###  Delete

sql
DELETE FROM Students 
WHERE Student_id = 11;



## Important Queries

###  Students enrolled after 2022

sql
SELECT * FROM Students 
WHERE Enrollment_date > '2022-12-31';


###  Courses from Mathematics department

sql
SELECT c.* 
FROM Courses c
JOIN Departments d 
ON c.Department_id = d.Department_id
WHERE d.Department_name = 'mathematics'
LIMIT 5;


### Students in both SQL and Data Structures

sql
SELECT s.student_id, s.firstname 
FROM Students s
JOIN Enrollments e ON s.student_id = e.student_id
WHERE e.course_id IN (101,102)
GROUP BY s.student_id, s.firstname
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT e.course_id) = 2;


###  Total students per course

sql
SELECT course_id, COUNT(student_id) AS total_students
FROM Enrollments
GROUP BY course_id;

##  Joins Used

### Inner Join

sql
SELECT s.firstname, c.course_name 
FROM Students s
JOIN Enrollments e ON s.student_id = e.student_id
JOIN Courses c ON e.course_id = c.course_id;


### Left Join

sql
SELECT s.firstname, c.course_name
FROM Students s
LEFT JOIN Enrollments e ON s.student_id = e.student_id
LEFT JOIN Courses c ON e.course_id = c.course_id;



## Advanced Queries

### Average Credits

sql
SELECT AVG(credits) FROM Courses;


###  Max Salary in Computer Science

sql
SELECT MAX(i.salary)
FROM Instructors i
JOIN Departments d ON i.Department_id = d.Department_id


###  Running Total of Students

sql
SELECT course_id,
COUNT(student_id),
SUM(COUNT(student_id)) OVER (ORDER BY course_id)
FROM Enrollments
GROUP BY course_id;




## Student Classification

sql
SELECT student_id, firstname,
CASE
    WHEN Enrollment_date <= DATE_SUB(CURDATE(), INTERVAL 4 YEAR) THEN 'Senior'
    ELSE 'Junior'
END AS status
FROM Students;




